{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Progression Curve.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Progression Curve.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"progression curve progression curve","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Progression Curve.md","fileName":"Progression Curve.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Progression Curve","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 14:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Game Balance and Progression]] [[Game Challenge Design]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Balance and Progression","Game Challenge Design","Designer Loop","Playtesting","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Progression Curve.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Progression Curve.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"progression curve progression curve","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Progression Curve.md","fileName":"Progression Curve.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Progression Curve","heading":"Progression Curve","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A progression curve maps increases in cost to increases in benefit or power over time. It regulates the rate at which challenges, rewards, attributes, and thresholds change so the player continues to feel advancement.\n\nLinear, polynomial, exponential, logistic, piecewise-linear, and hand-crafted curves create different pacing and psychological effects. The mathematical shape is a starting structure that must be adjusted through the [[Designer Loop]] and [[Playtesting]].\n\nPerceived challenge may follow a zigzag rather than a smooth rise. A new demand can temporarily push the player toward frustration, while mastery and a quieter section create a plateau before the next development.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Balance and Progression","Game Challenge Design","Designer Loop","Playtesting","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Progression Curve.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Progression Curve.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"progression curve progression curve","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Progression Curve.md","fileName":"Progression Curve.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Progression Curve","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[advancedgamedesign.pdf]]\n[[agamedesignvocabulary.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Balance and Progression","Game Challenge Design","Designer Loop","Playtesting","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}